# GaitGuard — macbook-demo

Quickstart (macOS)

1. Clone and checkout demo branch:
   git fetch origin
   git checkout macbook-demo

2. Create & activate venv:
   python3 -m venv .venv
   source .venv/bin/activate

3. Install deps:
   pip install -r requirements.txt
   pip install certifi  # ensures mediapipe model download works on macOS

4. Ensure directories exist and create .env if needed:
   mkdir -p notebooks docs logs
   cp .env.example .env

5. Run the demo:
   # add src to PYTHONPATH or run demo directly (demo already auto-adds src to sys.path)
   python src/demos/demo_camera.py --fps 5

Notes:
- The demo uses MediaPipe Pose. On first run mediapipe downloads its TFLite model (requires internet).
- The baseline uses a warm-up of 10 embeddings per worker before scoring begins.
- The demo buffers timeseries rows and flushes to SQLite every 10s to avoid frequent DB writes.
- To quit the demo window press `q`.